/-!
# (C3)*'s numerals: the height cells and their anchors

Generated by a script.

The partition `RMF.c3Theta` of `ϑ ∈ [0, 1]` into 24 cells (ends in units of `1/320`,
finest at `ϑ = 0`, where every `q`-interval's minimum sits), and at each end `ϑ_j` the
anchors of `RMF.le_c3Val_of`: `cosExpAnti(-ϑ_j) - cosExpAnti(-1-ϑ_j)` bracketed by
`interval_decide` on the Horner form (`RMF.c3AnchorLo_j`, `RMF.c3AnchorHi_j`) and
`e^{-ϑ_j} ≤ Y_j` by Taylor's lower sums (`RMF.c3AnchorY_j`).
-/

